# =============================================================================
# `.gitignore` for `asynchronous-release-telemetry-engine`
#
# Purpose : keep local noise out of the repository and protect the canonical
#           tree defined in `README.md` Section 7.
# Pattern : general ignores first, then two allow-lists (`data/` and `assets/`)
#           where an accidental commit could leak real or personal content.
# Note    : an ignored file can still be committed deliberately with
#           `git add -f <path>`. Use that only after reading Section 6 and 7.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. `Python` bytecode and tool caches
#    `src/triage_parser.py` is standard-library only, so caches appear only
#    when tools or other scripts import it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Virtual and `conda` environments
#    The documented environment `telemetry-engine` is created by `conda` outside
#    this folder. These entries cover environments created inside it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
.conda/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Workspace configuration overrides
#    `VS Code` stores the selected interpreter and local settings in `.vscode/`;
#    these are machine-specific and are not part of the deliverable.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Operating-system files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Scratch files and processing artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp
*~


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. DATA GUARD (privacy boundary, `README.md` Section 11)
#    Only the two canonical data files are tracked. Anything else placed in
#    these folders, including a real feedback export, stays local.
#    The folders themselves are not ignored, so the allow-list entries work.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/*
!data/raw/feedback_export_sample.json

data/processed/*
!data/processed/triaged_feedback.csv


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. EVIDENCE GUARD (`README.md` Section 10)
#    Only the five named screenshots are tracked. Screenshots of
#    `Jira Product Discovery` and `Confluence` can show account names, email
#    addresses, and site addresses. Redact them, name them exactly as below,
#    and the allow-list will pick them up.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/*
!assets/jpd_matrix_view.png
!assets/jpd_list_view.png
!assets/confluence_prd_page.png
!assets/parser_run.png
!assets/jpd_automation_audit.png


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Secrets guard
#    No credentials are used by this repository. These entries protect against
#    a future `Atlassian` API token or key being committed by accident.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
